  "id": "COMPOUND:22364 - PROTEIN:4930",
  "verbalization": "Abrusoside D is shown to interact with Integrin beta-6, which is a target of multiple compounds, including 2-Phenyl-propane-1,1-diol diacetate and (1S,2R,3R,9S,10S)-1,10-dihydroxy-12-methyl-2,9-bis(prop-1-en-2-yl)-4,14-dioxatricyclo[9.2.1.13,6]pentadeca-6(15),11-diene-5,13-dione. All these compounds are linked to the Small conductance calcium-activated potassium channel protein 1, suggesting a potential mechanism where Abrusoside D may modulate this channel through the interaction with Integrin beta-6. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, indicating a possible role in the regulation of calcium signaling through integrin-mediated pathways. The mechanism is supported by the presence of multiple targets in the same pathway, which implies a potential role in cellular processes involving calcium homeostasis and signaling. The integration of these pathways suggests that Abrusoside D may exert its effects through a mechanism involving integrin beta-6 and subsequent calcium-activated potassium channel activity, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction and functional role.",
